1
00:00:04,963 --> 00:00:10,385
RAPID INCREASE
IN FOREIGN TOURISTS IN JAPAN!

2
00:01:01,686 --> 00:01:05,356
Foreign tourists have it so good,
living in luxury.

3
00:01:05,440 --> 00:01:07,317
We Japanese

4
00:01:07,400 --> 00:01:11,112
don't have the time or the money
to be talking about vacations!

5
00:01:13,364 --> 00:01:15,867
When would you like to make
your next appointment?

6
00:01:15,950 --> 00:01:17,160
Let's see…

7
00:01:17,243 --> 00:01:20,080
How about next Wednesday at 4:00 p.m.?

8
00:01:20,163 --> 00:01:21,539
Yes, that's available.

9
00:01:21,623 --> 00:01:23,291
So, on the 22nd--

10
00:01:23,374 --> 00:01:25,668
Wait, no.
I have a nail appointment that day.

11
00:01:25,752 --> 00:01:27,962
Would you like to choose another day?

12
00:01:28,046 --> 00:01:30,340
How about Thursday afternoon?

13
00:01:30,924 --> 00:01:32,675
Okay, 5:00 p.m. is available.

14
00:01:32,759 --> 00:01:34,093
Let's go with that.

15
00:01:34,177 --> 00:01:37,972
Understood, I will book you in
for the 23rd at 5:00 p.m.

16
00:01:38,056 --> 00:01:39,766
- Oh, not on the 23rd.
- What?

17
00:01:40,934 --> 00:01:44,979
I see. Our other available times are--

18
00:01:45,063 --> 00:01:45,855
Midori.

19
00:01:47,857 --> 00:01:49,692
Please excuse me for a moment.

20
00:01:50,944 --> 00:01:53,988
Did we have an appointment
for Ms. Yamada today?

21
00:01:54,072 --> 00:01:55,031
What?

22
00:01:55,115 --> 00:01:56,157
Ms. Yamada?

23
00:01:56,241 --> 00:01:57,742
Did you double-book?

24
00:01:57,826 --> 00:01:59,202
She's here right now,

25
00:01:59,285 --> 00:02:02,872
but the doctor is performing
a procedure on another patient.

26
00:02:02,956 --> 00:02:03,915
What?

27
00:02:08,545 --> 00:02:10,046
Excuse me.

28
00:02:10,964 --> 00:02:14,551
I'm very sorry.
I will go check on this right away.

29
00:02:17,303 --> 00:02:19,264
Hello, this is Lachulia Beauty Clinic.

30
00:02:19,347 --> 00:02:21,850
<i>I'm sorry,</i>
<i>I can't make my appointment today.</i>

31
00:02:21,933 --> 00:02:24,686
- Oh, yes… Well…
<i>- Can I reschedule it to tomorrow?</i>

32
00:02:24,769 --> 00:02:27,522
May I have your name
and appointment time--

33
00:02:27,605 --> 00:02:28,565
Excuse me.

34
00:02:28,648 --> 00:02:30,358
- Yes?
- Take my appointment first.

35
00:02:30,441 --> 00:02:33,236
- Yes, please hold on for just a moment.
- When are you open?

36
00:02:33,319 --> 00:02:34,612
- Excuse me!
- Yes?

37
00:02:35,613 --> 00:02:37,407
Well, let's see…

38
00:02:37,490 --> 00:02:39,784
- Is Wednesday at 6:00 p.m. available?
- Wednesday?

39
00:02:39,868 --> 00:02:41,202
Please hold on a moment.

40
00:02:41,286 --> 00:02:42,287
I'm very sorry.

41
00:02:42,370 --> 00:02:44,038
- Midori.
- It's the only day that works.

42
00:02:44,122 --> 00:02:45,165
Yes, I understand.

43
00:02:45,248 --> 00:02:47,000
- 6:00 p.m.
- Wednesday?

44
00:02:47,083 --> 00:02:48,126
- Let's see…
- Midori.

45
00:02:48,209 --> 00:02:49,252
Yes!

46
00:02:49,335 --> 00:02:51,087
- Oh…
- Can I get the appointment?

47
00:02:51,170 --> 00:02:52,255
- I understand.
- Midori.

48
00:02:52,338 --> 00:02:53,464
Yes…

49
00:03:00,138 --> 00:03:02,432
RAPID INCREASE
IN FOREIGN TOURISTS IN JAPAN!

50
00:03:02,515 --> 00:03:04,517
It's the same thing, every day,

51
00:03:05,184 --> 00:03:08,021
constant appointment changes
and last-minute cancellations.

52
00:03:08,104 --> 00:03:10,023
I feel like I'm going crazy!

53
00:03:11,941 --> 00:03:14,319
Midori! Change the channel.

54
00:03:14,402 --> 00:03:15,695
Our clinic is on.

55
00:03:17,196 --> 00:03:18,489
<i>The case of</i>

56
00:03:18,573 --> 00:03:21,576
<i>Dr. Mieko Matsukawa, the director</i>
<i>of Lachulia Beauty Clinic in Shinjuku,</i>

57
00:03:21,659 --> 00:03:22,994
<i>has been sent to prosecutors.</i>

58
00:03:23,077 --> 00:03:24,704
- What?
<i>- According to the police…</i>

59
00:03:24,787 --> 00:03:25,955
The director?

60
00:03:26,039 --> 00:03:27,206
What? Why?

61
00:03:27,290 --> 00:03:28,708
<i>…provided cosmetic treatments</i>

62
00:03:28,791 --> 00:03:31,377
<i>by using unapproved drugs</i>
<i>and surgical methods on patients.</i>

63
00:03:31,461 --> 00:03:33,171
<i>An order to suspend operations…</i>

64
00:03:33,254 --> 00:03:35,048
An order to suspend operations?

65
00:03:35,131 --> 00:03:38,509
Wait, what's going to happen
to our clinic?

66
00:03:39,010 --> 00:03:43,056
<i>Several clients have spoken out</i>
<i>on social media</i>

67
00:03:43,139 --> 00:03:44,682
<i>about receiving surgery</i>…

68
00:03:44,766 --> 00:03:45,934
Konta?

69
00:03:46,017 --> 00:03:47,018
KONTA

70
00:03:47,685 --> 00:03:48,728
Hello?

71
00:03:48,811 --> 00:03:51,689
<i>Hey, Midori. I'm about to shoot a drama.</i>

72
00:03:51,773 --> 00:03:53,900
<i>This is my dressing room!</i>

73
00:03:53,983 --> 00:03:55,401
Hey, Konta, things are bad.

74
00:03:55,485 --> 00:03:58,488
The clinic I work at might go under.

75
00:03:58,571 --> 00:04:00,657
I might end up unemployed.

76
00:04:01,241 --> 00:04:04,994
<i>Whoa, that's great news, Midori!</i>

77
00:04:05,078 --> 00:04:07,455
<i>You've been saying</i>
<i>you want to quit your job forever!</i>

78
00:04:07,538 --> 00:04:10,500
<i>Well, that's true, but…</i>

79
00:04:10,583 --> 00:04:11,751
Oh, Konta.

80
00:04:11,834 --> 00:04:14,212
Oh, Mr. Jin, hello!

81
00:04:14,295 --> 00:04:15,255
JIN ICHIJO

82
00:04:15,338 --> 00:04:17,632
So? Are you in this drama?

83
00:04:17,715 --> 00:04:18,675
Any lines?

84
00:04:18,758 --> 00:04:21,511
I'm just a background patient today.

85
00:04:22,220 --> 00:04:24,430
Oh, you're an extra?

86
00:04:25,139 --> 00:04:26,683
- Hang in there.
- Thank you.

87
00:04:27,767 --> 00:04:29,435
I look forward to working with you!

88
00:04:29,519 --> 00:04:30,353
Thanks.

89
00:04:30,436 --> 00:04:31,479
Thank you.

90
00:04:32,647 --> 00:04:34,065
JIN ICHIJO

91
00:04:35,608 --> 00:04:37,110
KONTA HOSHINO

92
00:04:37,193 --> 00:04:38,444
Sorry about that.

93
00:04:38,528 --> 00:04:42,365
Mr. Jin, the lead actor, just came by,
so we were discussing work.

94
00:04:42,949 --> 00:04:46,828
<i>So then, doesn't that mean you can</i>
<i>take a break for a while?</i>

95
00:04:46,911 --> 00:04:49,706
Well, instead of a while,
it might be forever.

96
00:04:50,373 --> 00:04:53,293
Then you can go you know where.

97
00:04:53,376 --> 00:04:55,044
Grandma's villa!

98
00:04:55,670 --> 00:04:56,587
Oh…

99
00:04:57,255 --> 00:04:58,298
You're right.

100
00:05:03,970 --> 00:05:05,638
THREE DAYS LATER

101
00:05:12,562 --> 00:05:14,480
All right! Cleaning supplies, check!

102
00:05:14,564 --> 00:05:16,899
Change of clothes, check!
Toilet paper, check!

103
00:05:16,983 --> 00:05:18,026
Towels, check!

104
00:05:18,109 --> 00:05:20,862
Meat, check! Snacks, check!
Alcohol, check!

105
00:05:20,945 --> 00:05:22,488
Shall we go then?

106
00:05:22,989 --> 00:05:24,282
On our…

107
00:05:24,365 --> 00:05:26,200
Vacation!

108
00:05:28,786 --> 00:05:30,455
What? Yeah, it's this way.

109
00:05:38,463 --> 00:05:40,173
This feels great.

110
00:05:40,965 --> 00:05:42,216
This is too much walking!

111
00:05:42,300 --> 00:05:44,385
- It's a seagull!
- A seagull!

112
00:05:44,469 --> 00:05:46,763
Oh, someone is fishing!

113
00:05:46,846 --> 00:05:48,848
Are you catching anything?

114
00:05:48,931 --> 00:05:50,933
Hey, stop it, that's embarrassing.

115
00:05:51,017 --> 00:05:52,101
What are you doing?

116
00:05:52,185 --> 00:05:54,312
The villa is that way. Let's go.

117
00:05:56,230 --> 00:05:58,399
Oh, wait! It says "Villa Grounds"!

118
00:05:58,483 --> 00:06:00,234
You're right! Then it's this way.

119
00:06:00,318 --> 00:06:01,360
Yeah.

120
00:06:02,236 --> 00:06:03,613
Whoa.

121
00:06:05,031 --> 00:06:06,365
Hello.

122
00:06:07,366 --> 00:06:08,910
Hello.

123
00:06:09,494 --> 00:06:10,703
Hey.

124
00:06:13,498 --> 00:06:15,166
Chainsaw Woman?

125
00:06:16,250 --> 00:06:17,794
What's that?

126
00:06:17,877 --> 00:06:21,380
A woman who is a Chainsaw Man,
therefore Chainsaw Woman?

127
00:06:21,464 --> 00:06:24,509
So that's a Chainsaw Woman?

128
00:06:24,592 --> 00:06:26,844
- Are you a Chainsaw Woman?
- Be quiet!

129
00:06:27,678 --> 00:06:29,764
This is tough! So tough!

130
00:06:29,847 --> 00:06:32,058
Hey, what are you doing?

131
00:06:32,934 --> 00:06:35,019
Konta, look! The ocean!

132
00:06:35,937 --> 00:06:37,480
Wow, it's so close!

133
00:06:37,563 --> 00:06:39,398
- It's a slope, it's dangerous!
- Watch out!

134
00:06:39,482 --> 00:06:42,193
Konta, be careful!

135
00:06:42,276 --> 00:06:43,611
You got it?

136
00:06:43,694 --> 00:06:45,696
- I got it open.
- I'll take it.

137
00:06:50,118 --> 00:06:52,703
- We made it!
- Awesome!

138
00:06:52,787 --> 00:06:56,124
Are you catching anything?

139
00:06:56,207 --> 00:06:57,416
He can't hear you.

140
00:06:58,793 --> 00:07:00,336
Let's take a picture.

141
00:07:00,419 --> 00:07:01,587
Yeah, let's do it!

142
00:07:01,671 --> 00:07:02,839
Okay, here we go.

143
00:07:02,922 --> 00:07:04,632
- Okay!
- Say cheese!

144
00:07:04,715 --> 00:07:05,716
Yay!

145
00:07:05,800 --> 00:07:06,843
All right.

146
00:07:08,177 --> 00:07:11,055
- Wow, awesome!
- It's huge!

147
00:07:14,767 --> 00:07:16,644
The kitchen is amazing too!

148
00:07:17,979 --> 00:07:19,856
- What?
- The sofa is giant!

149
00:07:20,857 --> 00:07:22,316
So fluffy!

150
00:07:22,817 --> 00:07:24,277
This is insane!

151
00:07:24,360 --> 00:07:27,572
To think this view is all ours.

152
00:07:27,655 --> 00:07:30,324
That's right, it belongs to us,
brother and sister!

153
00:07:30,408 --> 00:07:32,326
Forward roll on the sofa!

154
00:07:39,750 --> 00:07:42,128
I heard that after Grandma
divorced Grandpa,

155
00:07:42,211 --> 00:07:44,505
she became estranged
from our Hoshino family,

156
00:07:44,589 --> 00:07:48,009
but she remarried a really
wealthy man and built this villa.

157
00:07:48,092 --> 00:07:49,760
Grandma was amazing!

158
00:07:49,844 --> 00:07:50,678
That's right.

159
00:07:50,761 --> 00:07:52,472
And since Grandma passed away,

160
00:07:52,555 --> 00:07:55,850
the relatives on that side
haven't been using it lately,

161
00:07:55,933 --> 00:07:58,227
so we get to use it!

162
00:07:58,311 --> 00:07:59,687
Yay!

163
00:08:03,566 --> 00:08:05,610
Hey! Look at that.

164
00:08:06,194 --> 00:08:07,111
Look!

165
00:08:09,363 --> 00:08:10,823
It's really something.

166
00:08:12,825 --> 00:08:14,035
- Let's go?
- Yes.

167
00:08:14,118 --> 00:08:15,119
Come on!

168
00:08:16,037 --> 00:08:17,079
All right!

169
00:08:17,163 --> 00:08:20,124
- Wow!
- The yard is huge!

170
00:08:21,417 --> 00:08:24,504
Okay, there we go!

171
00:08:24,587 --> 00:08:25,630
All done.

172
00:08:30,718 --> 00:08:32,512
- Amazing!
- It's surprisingly steep!

173
00:08:32,595 --> 00:08:34,764
- Wait up!
- Be careful!

174
00:08:34,847 --> 00:08:37,266
- Come on!
- It's surprisingly steep! Watch out!

175
00:08:37,350 --> 00:08:39,268
Konta, summer oranges!

176
00:08:39,352 --> 00:08:40,520
Awesome!

177
00:08:41,020 --> 00:08:43,064
I wonder if Grandma liked summer oranges.

178
00:08:43,147 --> 00:08:45,024
Wow, there are so many.

179
00:08:45,107 --> 00:08:46,317
Grandma…

180
00:08:47,318 --> 00:08:49,111
If we sold all of these,
how much would we earn?

181
00:08:49,195 --> 00:08:50,112
Konta!

182
00:08:50,196 --> 00:08:52,365
I was just praying to Grandma in heaven!

183
00:08:53,074 --> 00:08:53,950
That's right.

184
00:08:54,033 --> 00:08:56,786
We don't have a Buddhist altar here,
but I should pray.

185
00:08:57,453 --> 00:09:01,165
Thank you, Grandma,
for leaving us such a wonderful villa.

186
00:09:02,875 --> 00:09:05,253
We will take good care of it, Grandma.

187
00:09:05,336 --> 00:09:07,421
Well, want to try one?

188
00:09:07,505 --> 00:09:09,006
- All right.
- Let's!

189
00:09:09,090 --> 00:09:11,217
They're really big. How about that one?

190
00:09:11,300 --> 00:09:12,510
- Should I grab it?
- Yes!

191
00:09:18,683 --> 00:09:20,017
So sour! What is this?

192
00:09:20,101 --> 00:09:23,271
I know. When I cut it open,
it was so sour, I couldn't eat it.

193
00:09:23,354 --> 00:09:25,773
We can't sell these.
They're as sour as lemons.

194
00:09:25,856 --> 00:09:27,900
We can use them
as a substitute for lemons.

195
00:09:27,984 --> 00:09:29,694
For cooking or making sour drinks.

196
00:09:29,777 --> 00:09:32,738
And this leftover thick peel…

197
00:09:34,949 --> 00:09:36,367
can be used for cleaning!

198
00:09:36,450 --> 00:09:38,661
You're so impressive, Midori!

199
00:09:38,744 --> 00:09:40,204
You're good at cleaning and cooking,

200
00:09:40,288 --> 00:09:43,416
and your face is cute like mine,
so why don't you have a boyfriend?

201
00:09:44,000 --> 00:09:45,585
You don't have a girlfriend either.

202
00:09:47,086 --> 00:09:48,045
Well, that's true.

203
00:09:49,297 --> 00:09:51,966
To think we would end up
spending a vacation together

204
00:09:52,049 --> 00:09:54,093
at such a wonderful seaside villa.

205
00:09:54,176 --> 00:09:57,471
It's not really a vacation for you…
Aren't you unemployed?

206
00:09:57,555 --> 00:09:58,764
What?

207
00:09:58,848 --> 00:10:00,516
Stop putting it so unromantically!

208
00:10:00,600 --> 00:10:01,809
My bad, sorry.

209
00:10:11,611 --> 00:10:14,113
Since no one had been here for a while,

210
00:10:14,196 --> 00:10:18,826
I thought it would be more overgrown,
but it's actually pretty well-maintained.

211
00:10:19,493 --> 00:10:20,536
All right…

212
00:10:37,261 --> 00:10:38,387
Hello.

213
00:10:40,139 --> 00:10:42,224
H-Hello.

214
00:10:43,726 --> 00:10:44,769
Who are you?

215
00:10:46,687 --> 00:10:50,733
I'm the granddaughter
of the owner of this villa.

216
00:10:51,400 --> 00:10:53,235
You can call me Hoshino.

217
00:10:53,903 --> 00:10:56,781
This is the villa
of my late grandmother, Nobuko.

218
00:10:57,448 --> 00:10:59,992
Oh, Ms. Nobuko.

219
00:11:06,082 --> 00:11:10,252
Because this villa
is near the ocean, the wind…

220
00:11:12,129 --> 00:11:14,715
can be very strong at times.

221
00:11:16,300 --> 00:11:17,176
Oh.

222
00:11:18,302 --> 00:11:19,178
Got it.

223
00:11:20,221 --> 00:11:21,722
Look, here it is again.

224
00:11:32,358 --> 00:11:34,110
S-So handsome.

225
00:11:35,152 --> 00:11:37,405
Midori! I found a drone beetle!

226
00:11:37,488 --> 00:11:39,907
Vroom! A drone beetle…

227
00:11:39,990 --> 00:11:41,158
Wow, a handsome guy.

228
00:11:43,160 --> 00:11:44,537
Nice to meet you.

229
00:11:44,620 --> 00:11:47,373
I manage these villa grounds.

230
00:11:48,374 --> 00:11:51,168
I'm the caretaker, Nishigami.

231
00:11:51,752 --> 00:11:53,754
Oh, the caretaker.

232
00:11:53,838 --> 00:11:55,339
I see.

233
00:11:55,423 --> 00:11:58,008
So there's someone like that here.
That's convenient.

234
00:11:58,092 --> 00:12:01,971
We haven't been here since we were kids,
so we have no idea how things work.

235
00:12:02,847 --> 00:12:04,890
Oh, this is my brother.

236
00:12:04,974 --> 00:12:06,434
My older brother, Konta.

237
00:12:06,517 --> 00:12:07,476
I'm Konta.

238
00:12:07,560 --> 00:12:08,727
Mr. Konta.

239
00:12:10,020 --> 00:12:10,938
And you are?

240
00:12:12,523 --> 00:12:14,733
Well, I'm Midori.

241
00:12:14,817 --> 00:12:16,652
My name is Midori Hoshino.

242
00:12:18,195 --> 00:12:19,238
Ms. Midori.

243
00:12:19,321 --> 00:12:20,364
Yes.

244
00:12:22,992 --> 00:12:27,997
Are you planning to spend
your time off at this villa?

245
00:12:28,080 --> 00:12:32,334
Yes. They said on TV
that Japanese people aren't good

246
00:12:32,418 --> 00:12:33,794
at taking vacations.

247
00:12:33,878 --> 00:12:35,212
- They did say that.
- Yeah.

248
00:12:35,296 --> 00:12:38,466
So we thought we would try taking
one of those things called a vacation.

249
00:12:38,549 --> 00:12:39,425
That's right.

250
00:12:39,508 --> 00:12:40,509
Yes.

251
00:12:42,178 --> 00:12:43,721
A vacation…

252
00:13:00,613 --> 00:13:01,989
Midori Hoshino.

253
00:13:02,823 --> 00:13:04,158
Konta Hoshino.

254
00:13:22,551 --> 00:13:24,094
<i>Did you call for me?</i>

255
00:13:24,178 --> 00:13:26,931
<i>I am the Grim Reaper</i>
<i>in charge of Tatsumi Town.</i>

256
00:13:27,848 --> 00:13:31,685
<i>Is there anything to report from</i>
<i>the Shiokaze district of Tatsumi Town?</i>

257
00:13:32,937 --> 00:13:34,897
No. Nothing in particular.

258
00:13:36,649 --> 00:13:39,527
<i>Those villa grounds</i>
<i>are under your jurisdiction.</i>

259
00:13:39,610 --> 00:13:41,487
<i>You do know that in one month,</i>

260
00:13:41,570 --> 00:13:46,325
<i>a landslide caused by a massive typhoon</i>
<i>will kill all the residents, correct?</i>

261
00:13:48,536 --> 00:13:49,620
Yes.

262
00:14:00,422 --> 00:14:04,426
Konta! Summer orange juice! Try it!

263
00:14:04,510 --> 00:14:05,886
- What? You made it into juice?
- Yes!

264
00:14:05,970 --> 00:14:07,054
Thanks, Midori.

265
00:14:07,137 --> 00:14:08,847
- You're welcome.
- Down the hatch.

266
00:14:10,140 --> 00:14:10,975
So sour!

267
00:14:11,058 --> 00:14:11,934
Gross!

268
00:14:12,017 --> 00:14:14,270
- It's sour! What is this?
- You fell for it!

269
00:14:14,353 --> 00:14:15,563
Hey, Midori!

270
00:14:15,646 --> 00:14:17,439
Midori, wait up!

271
00:14:17,523 --> 00:14:18,732
Watch out!

272
00:14:18,816 --> 00:14:22,027
- Stay back!
- Here it comes, bam!

273
00:14:23,070 --> 00:14:25,364
- Here I go!
- Come at me!

274
00:14:25,447 --> 00:14:27,658
Are you or are you not?

275
00:14:27,741 --> 00:14:28,742
No!

276
00:14:28,826 --> 00:14:31,745
Hey, this area is mine!

277
00:14:31,829 --> 00:14:33,581
- My area!
- Stop!

278
00:14:33,664 --> 00:14:35,165
This is mine!

279
00:14:53,267 --> 00:14:54,935
Yes?

280
00:14:55,019 --> 00:14:56,395
- We came.
- We came.

281
00:14:56,979 --> 00:14:59,982
Wow! What is this place?
It's absolutely amazing!

282
00:15:00,649 --> 00:15:02,234
<i>This is my friend, Tetsuro.</i>

283
00:15:02,318 --> 00:15:04,486
A barbecue needs a man's strength!

284
00:15:04,570 --> 00:15:05,571
Huh?

285
00:15:05,654 --> 00:15:07,740
More people are here.

286
00:15:07,823 --> 00:15:09,325
<i>Who is this handsome guy?</i>

287
00:15:09,408 --> 00:15:12,036
<i>This is Mr. Nishigami,</i>
<i>who takes care of the villas around here.</i>

288
00:15:14,371 --> 00:15:16,081
Vacations are the best!

289
00:15:16,165 --> 00:15:17,291
The best!

290
00:15:17,875 --> 00:15:20,252
<i>Let's all spend this summer here together!</i>

291
00:15:20,836 --> 00:15:23,631
<i>Until the moment</i>
<i>the flame of their lives goes out,</i>

292
00:15:24,298 --> 00:15:26,759
I will watch over them closely.

293
00:15:28,344 --> 00:15:29,303
Subtitle translation by: Maslin F.
